Apply order 0023 against mariopartyrd/partyboard 98ac07fd1e8f7ab938bbb6fe75789fad99419010 (CC0-1.0; ADR 0009 section 5).
m423Dll: no VECAdd into the arg3 pointer's own stack slot, on MPT_PC
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/mp4/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

In Goooooooal (m423), fn_1_137C4 ends each of its six hit cases with
VECAdd((Vec *)&arg3, &sp10, (Vec *)&arg3): it adds to the bytes of the pointer arg3, not to the
vector it points at. On the console that writes 12 bytes over a 4-byte stack slot and neighbours the
function never reads again, so the game is unaffected. The module is built for 64 bits with /GS:
the slot is 8 bytes, the write runs into the stack cookie and the function fails fast on return
(0xC0000409). Seed 1's party autopilot stopped there in turn 19 (M4-01, docs/titles/mp4.md
section 21). On MPT_PC the call is left out, which keeps the console's behaviour: the call never
changed *arg3.

